From 9f74e64ecbbbd53164924dc3d578a38dca9f6c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fady <fadyackad@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:58:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] apps_std: serve fopen, fwrite, fsync, fremove, ftrunc and
 frename

Implement the apps_std methods the sensor framework's registry initialisation calls (ids as in quic/fastrpc inc/apps_std.h: fopen 0, fwrite 5, fsync 23, fremove 24, ftrunc 32, frename 33; ids above 30 travel in the first primitive word), open w/a/+ modes read-write, and let fopen_with_env open an absolute name whatever search variable the DSP names. Refusing the first write (fremove, then fopen of the DIR marker for writing) made the X1E80100 firmware assert in sns_registry_sensor.c and take the whole ADSP down. Unlike the stubs proposed in pull request 21, the writes reach the files, so what the framework persists (its parsed registry, calibration) is there at the next start.

Link: https://github.com/linux-msm/hexagonrpc/issues/19

Link: https://github.com/linux-msm/hexagonrpc/pull/21
---
 hexagonrpcd/apps_std.c           | 299 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 hexagonrpcd/interface/apps_std.c |  79 ++++++++
 hexagonrpcd/interface/apps_std.h |   6 +
 3 files changed, 311 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)

